 > SELECT Token FROM Sessions JOIN Bots ON Sessions.UserId = Bots.UserId AND Bots.OwnerId = 'com.mattermost.calls' ORDER BY Sessions.CreateAt DESC LIMIT 1;
 > ```
 
+## Transcription backends
+
+Transcription is performed locally by [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp) by default. The backend is selected through the `TRANSCRIBE_API` environment variable:
+
+| Value | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `whisper.cpp` (default) | Local whisper.cpp. Audio never leaves the container. |
+| `azure` | Azure Cognitive Services Speech. |
+| `openai/api` | A remote, OpenAI compatible `/v1/audio/transcriptions` endpoint. |
+
+### OpenAI compatible API backend
+
+> **_Warning_**
+>
+> Selecting `TRANSCRIBE_API=openai/api` **uploads the recorded call audio to a third party service**. Anyone self-hosting Mattermost to keep call content on their own infrastructure loses that guarantee the moment this backend is enabled: the audio of every participant is sent to whichever endpoint `OPENAI_API_BASE_URL` points at, subject to that provider's retention and training policies. Keep the default `whisper.cpp` backend unless you have explicitly accepted this trade-off, and point `OPENAI_API_BASE_URL` at a service you control if you need the extra accuracy without the exposure.
+
+This backend works with any service implementing OpenAI's `/v1/audio/transcriptions` endpoint (OpenAI, Groq, LocalAI, a self-hosted whisper server, ...). It is configured through the following variables, which can be passed either as environment variables on the job container or as keys of the `TRANSCRIBE_API_OPTIONS` JSON object:
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `OPENAI_API_BASE_URL` | `https://api.openai.com/v1` | The base URL of the API. `/audio/transcriptions` is appended to it. |
+| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | (empty) | The API key, sent as a `Bearer` token. Can be left empty for services that don't require authentication. It is never logged. |
+| `OPENAI_API_MODEL` | `whisper-1` | The transcription model to use (e.g. `whisper-large-v3` on Groq). |
+| `OPENAI_API_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `60` | Timeout for a single transcription request. |
+
+Example:
+
+```
+docker run --network=host --name calls-transcriber -e "SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8065/" -e "AUTH_TOKEN=ohqd1phqtt8m3gsfg8j5ymymqy" -e "CALL_ID=9c86b3q57fgfpqr8jq3b9yjweh" -e "POST_ID=e4pdmi6rqpn7pp9sity9hiza3r" -e "TRANSCRIBE_API=openai/api" -e "OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-..." -v calls-transcriber-volume:/recs mattermost/calls-transcriber
+```
+
+> **_Note_**
+>
+> - Requests are retried on transient failures (`408`, `429`, `5xx`, network errors). Authentication and other client errors are not retried.
+> - Audio longer than the API's upload limit (25MB, about 13 minutes of 16KHz mono audio) is split into chunks and the resulting timestamps are stitched back together. Splitting happens on a fixed size boundary so it may cut through a word.
+> - Live captions always use the local whisper.cpp models, regardless of this setting.
+> - If the service ignores the `verbose_json` response format and returns only the full text, a single segment spanning the whole audio chunk is produced instead of per-sentence timestamps.
+
 ### Development
 
 Run `make help` to see available options.
